    "content" : "I&#39;ve dug up some pictures from my homemade Gameboy cart, so here they are. The first one is mid-process of trying to solder the new ROM chip in place. The second photo is the cut out of the PCB that I dremel&#39;d to enable the PLCC holder to fit inside the cartridge case. The third photo shows the cut-out in the cartridge case to change out the ROM. It is hidden from view when used in a Gameboy/Gameboy Color. The fourth photo shows the AT49F040 ROM chip in place. The last photo shows the ridiculous wiring that needed to be completed to get this thing to function.",
    "objectType" : "note",
    "originalContent" : "I've dug up some pictures from my homemade Gameboy cart, so here they are. The first one is mid-process of trying to solder the new ROM chip in place. The second photo is the cut out of the PCB that I dremel'd to enable the PLCC holder to fit inside the cartridge case. The third photo shows the cut-out in the cartridge case to change out the ROM. It is hidden from view when used in a Gameboy/Gameboy Color. The fourth photo shows the AT49F040 ROM chip in place. The last photo shows the ridiculous wiring that needed to be completed to get this thing to function.",
